# Native holomorphic forms at the actual cusp of the constructed threefold

The original toric chart, exponential map, cusp quotient, and global
gluing comparison give the analytic vanishing extensions of all native
coefficients in Lemma 9.16(ii). All maps and derivatives use their original
complex atlases and genuine alternating tangent-covector pullbacks.
The exact factors are `(2πi)q`, `(2πi)^2 q`, and `(2πi)^3 q` in the positively
oriented reference chart, followed by the actual constant cusp-width
normalization. Each original coefficient has first analytic cusp order.
